  "loop_receipt_contract": "Each strict return freezes loop-receipt-v1 with immutable target, exact ordered issued-task snapshots, exact task/probe attribution, independently replayed active-at-decomposition state, and the prior accepted per-probe result. The same receipt must reach retained atoms/lineage/critic requests; evidence/world receive only their layer projection. Routing metadata is not evidence.",
  "adaptive_driver_contract": "A routed verification after round one requires a previously unseen eligible version returned through an active frozen verification probe's fetch/search task. Provenance-only, duplicate and reanalyse returns may update semantic or graph state but cannot trigger a second accuracy verification.",
  "followup_identity_contract": "One active task per (evidence/world, probe_id) slot. A new task atomically supersedes the prior task without a fabricated Resolution; superseded IDs are permanent tombstones across checkpoint resume and cannot reactivate.",
  "decisive_attribution_contract": "Headline label-change credit requires an exact-slot novel receipt and a frozen-plan counterfactual aggregate. Lineage uses target-terminal-path necessity, independence uses rooted-component necessity, and other conclusive probes require every newly added basis version to be an addressed exact-slot novel return. This is conservative structural attribution, not a retained semantic ablation run.",
  "paired_comparison_contract": "Fixed and routed arms share these exact files, baselines, prior artifacts, cases, model, budgets and repair caps. Their results are reported separately and never pooled. Fixed versus routed final accuracy is not a causal comparison because evidence exposure differs.",
  "gate": {
    "smoke": "p04, p07 and p08 must complete with no call, protocol, model, budget, hash, receipt, routing, graph, probe-delta or credential failure. Routed smoke must exercise at least one real probe-owned novel second pass; fixed smoke must retain exactly two verification cycles.",
    "full": "Only a passing same-arm smoke authorizes a fresh eight-case run. Require all scheduled cases retained, no label break against both baselines, exact v4 audits, and separately reported usage.",
    "failure_policy": "Preserve every failed directory. Do not overwrite, selectively complete, pool arms or change code/prompts/data/retry policy without a new freeze."
  },
